Students can work online or on a printed copy, and answers are due each Friday afternoon. Each student submits once, and each problem is worth 1point. Appearing on the leaderboard is a student\'92s choice. Teachers can see every solution from the start; students see a week's solutions once that week has closed. Teachers are not expected to grade the students work. The online submissions will be graded automatically while the papers will be collected every Friday and graded by an organizer. At the end of the 12 weeks the students that worked hard and consistently can be rewarded and acknowledged in some way (TBD).  }